title: Proof of Work
text: Gold does not turn corners, and all you have is the tool that breaks it apart. Every block must be finished before the next can begin. There are no shortcuts to the coin.
trick: only prisms: a yellow beam can never be turned whole, so to change direction it must be split, its red turned (a prism turns red 90 degrees), and merged again where red and green meet. The first block does this the short way; in the second the wall stops red on the near side, so it has to go all the way round and come back
motif: pictogram (a chain of two blocks, the coin below the last, a hood over each exit that fixes where each block must finish)
expect: merges>=2
---
L 2 2 2 y
T 4 14 0 y
*P 3 2 0 k
*P 3 6 4 k
*P 7 6 3 k
